; Once deep compiled recursion uses up the stack budget, a with-result call (`execute if function`,
; `execute store … run function`) is handed to vanilla. Only the callee's own `return` may reach the caller,
; like vanilla's function command: a callee that falls through is a failed condition and stores nothing,
; whatever its last command returned.
@setup
objective create t dummy

@function run
scoreboard players set #n t 0
scoreboard players set #hit t 0
scoreboard players set #s t -1
function mcfc-test:rec

@function rec
scoreboard players add #n t 1
execute if function mcfc-test:no_return run scoreboard players add #hit t 1
execute store result score #s t run function mcfc-test:no_return
execute if function mcfc-test:returns run scoreboard players add #ret t 1
execute if score #n t matches ..2999 run function mcfc-test:rec

@function no_return
scoreboard players add #c t 5

@function returns
scoreboard players add #c t 1
return 1

@validate
score #n t is 3000
score #hit t is 0
score #ret t is 3000
